 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? The paint appears darker because the pigment is scattered across a smooth layer of resin, rather than on the paper with the underlayer. It's annoying but harmless. You can lighten it with a little water and then it looks more like you'd expect. Use a sharpie as a layer under your painting. If it looks about right, you' done. If it looks too dark, you know you need to lighten it with water. Use a gloss varnish on top. It helps the pigment reflect light and makes the colours look brighter.",
